{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204849-hacked-cyborg-prototype-as-mage-wonder-spheres-and-augmentations","id":1204849,"title":"Hacked Cyborg Prototype as Mage - Wonder Spheres and Augmentations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-09T06:57:08-07:00","id":1204849,"title":"Hacked Cyborg Prototype as Mage - Wonder Spheres and Augmentations","content":"So a Progenitor prototype for an infiltrator cyborg line (specially designed to handle Reality Deviants, neutralizing them violently with minimal disruption) goes rogue after a VA it was sent to assassinate rewires its AI and frees it from the Technocracy's control. Pretty standard backstory for a &quot;synthetic&quot; Mage PC I imagine. Everything, from the AI and the neurological components and the biological parts and the machinery, all custom-made by a team of Progenitors.<br /> <br /> Would be great to have thoughts on the following:<br /> <br /> - SO many augmentations. It's a prototype, and the idea is to start big and then find finesse in later models, removing overly bulky and risky cybernetics. We're talking about a healing factor, nanites that repair machine components, reinforced endoskeleton, a primium mesh under the skin, enhanced physical attributes, enhanced senses. This thing was EXPENSIVE to make. And because it is meant for infiltration, this all had to be lovingly fused into a regular-looking human exterior. Certainly the passion project of a high-ranking individual who was owed a lot of favours.<br /> <br /> - This, of course, means SO much Permanent Paradox since the Cyborg has Awakened. This won't be a problem at first (I'll explain), but once he starts using Enlightened Procedures a botch could spell his undoing. At first he'll be relying on his augmentations and not using Sphere effects of course.<br /> <br /> - This brings us to Wonder Spheres. They aren't in M20, but I'm told they were in Revised. Essentially we're just halving the EXP cost of raising Spheres, but in exchange you can only work Magick through Wonders created with Prime 4. This means no Magick until Arete hits 4 and Prime is raised to 4, so that's a few sessions relying purely on a handgun, healing factor and an enhanced body. Since M20 has EXP costs for Wonders, I would politely ask the ST to waive this for such a niche and focused user of Wonders.<br /> <br /> - Part of the reason he would use them is concept. He's a special object, created scientifically, with unusual powers. That's a big part of what he is, even if it isn't who he is. Now if he's going to copy his creators, he'll be doing it with Wonders. They're like him, in a sense.<br /> <br /> - Furthermore, he's running hot with maybe 10 Permadox. You see him fast-casting anything, ever? Using anything Vulgar? That's a death sentence. So he's using Wonders to avoid those kinds of issues. Now of course botches are an issue, as is the consensus (a lot of scientific wonders are coincidental, but far from all), but it's much safer I should think.<br /> <br /> - Since subtlety was an important part of this prototype's development, he doesn't have wrist cannons or a cloaking device or anything like that. As a general rule, if it needs a special battery it's a no. The idea was that Deviants would find it easier to detect such enhancements (with the Prime Sphere, for example), making the model pointless. There was a somewhat childish streak of &quot;OKAY, NOW LET'S ADD PRIMIUM GUYS&quot; but this model is meant to embody subtlety. Therefore his only sources of Aggravated damage were external equipment provided by the Technocracy, which have degraded or been lost since he went rogue.<br /> <br /> - So what we're left with is a Prime 3 Matter 1 Life 1 Forces 1 Arete 3 Cyborg who can't actually use Magick (yet), with some extra health levels and boosted physical attributes, a healing factor, acute senses and some innate counter-magick, with training in espionage, combat and infiltration, carrying quite a lot of Permadox. Where does this fall within the curve of starting Mage PCs? Underpowered? Overpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:06:17-07:00","id":1204867,"title":"","content":"Depending on the other PCs.<br /> I tend to say slightly underpowered, but I would also point out that 10 Permadox is nowhere near a death sentence.<br /> Especially if you cast coincidental effects the Dox comes only into consideration if you botch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:12:17-07:00","id":1205272,"title":"","content":"I think it's a reasonable build. You may want a Defect to represent that the Technocracy wants to retrieve their asset <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I think there was a Hunted Defect in revised and in Book of Secrets)<br /> <br /> One thing, with Prime 3 you can create Charms. Wonders with limited uses. So you can do a little of potent magick at a cost. Also, since you don't have to roll to activate most Charms, those that are Coincident will never generate Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:07:02-07:00","id":1205378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204849-hacked-cyborg-prototype-as-mage-wonder-spheres-and-augmentations?p=1205272#post1205272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a reasonable build. You may want a Defect to represent that the Technocracy wants to retrieve their asset <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I think there was a Hunted Defect in revised and in Book of Secrets)<br /> <br /> One thing, with Prime 3 you can create Charms. Wonders with limited uses. So you can do a little of potent magick at a cost. Also, since you don't have to roll to activate most Charms, those that are Coincident will never generate Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I ended up going for something else, but it's still good information. Still don't quite understand Prime, Charms, Wonders etc. but I'll learn as I go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:24:52-07:00","id":1205385,"title":"","content":"Update: So the ST thinks that Wonder Spheres are slightly underpowered, but he refused it because he worried it would make the game less fun if I can't experience the flexibility of Magick. However he was fully on-board with the rest of it.<br /> <br /> Cyrus, or &quot;Psi&quot; (spelled with the Greek Letter Psi)<br /> <br /> Arete 3<br /> <br /> Prime 1 - Affinity - &quot;Primal Energetics&quot;<br /> Data 1 - &quot;Unified Field&quot;<br /> Matter 1 - &quot;Material Science&quot;<br /> Forces 1 - &quot;Lesser Energetics&quot;<br /> Mind 1 - &quot;Psionic Field&quot;<br /> Life 1 - &quot;Parabiology&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Everything is Data? Almost; a Mechanistic Cosmos has hardware too.<br /> <br /> A synergy of his physical cyborg nature and the virtual nature of his Awakening, Cyrus believes that the Universe is like a computer. All moving and static components are simulated through code, but that code MUST be supported by mechanistic hardware, the kind that supports his own AI. He believes that by understanding software (Computer) and hardware (Computer, Technology, Hyper-Tech) one can invoke the power of creation and shape the universe.<br /> <br /> Merits: Hands of Daedalus, Computer Aptitude, Mechanical Aptitude<br /> <br /> Flaws: Degeneration (6), Hit List (Progenitors), Probationary Sect Member<br /> <br /> Enhancements:<br /> <br /> - (10 Points) Primium Countermeasures. Gives 5 dice of counter-magick.<br /> <br /> - (3 Points) Onboard Computer. This is an upgraded version of the Enhancement which gives Internet Access. Instead this gives a compact but powerful computer (with internet access), suitable as a Focus for Sphere powers up to Level 3. I'm looking forward to completely invisibly using a computer while other VAs have to toy with their phones...<br /> <br /> - (2 Points) Reinforced Skeleton. Allows for other alterations, and gives 2 extra health levels.<br /> <br /> TT-00-01 was created as the 0th Generation Twin Threat prototype. A proof of concept, he was designed to eliminate dangerous Reality Deviants safely. He went rogue after a mysterious Virtual Adept broke down the conditioning programmed into his onboard computer. This led to his Awakening, turning him from a powerful Terminator style infiltrator into a novice Mage. Having lost most of his infiltration protocols (Stealth, Subterfuge and other relevant Abilities were higher while he was under Technocracy control) he has sided with the Traditions, specifically the Virtual Adepts. Since he is slowly dying (Degeneration; a proof of concept means corners are cut, and he only needed to live long enough to get funding for future units) he has to rely on his fellow Mages for support. Sadly his history as a Technocracy agent is common knowledge (Probationary Sect Member) meaning it will be an up-hill struggle. The Progenitors involved with Twin Threat wish to recover him, partly for practical reasons (recovering the expensive components) and partly for political reasons (appeasing the higher-ups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}